.TH INTERCOM-SATELLITE 1 "November 2026" "intercom-satellite 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
intercom-satellite \- intercom for Kiosk Satellite kiosks and phones
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B intercom-satellite
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Intercom Satellite Desktop App turns a Linux computer into an intercom for
Kiosk Satellite kiosks. It also works with the Intercom Satellite app on Android
phones: calls, video calls and announcements on the local network, optionally
encrypted with TLS.
It is an independent companion and not affiliated with Kiosk Satellite.
.PP
The window lists the kiosks found on the network over mDNS, or added by
address. Closing or minimizing the window keeps the intercom running in the
system tray, where
.B Quit
ends it.
.PP
Before the first call, enter the intercom key in
.BR Settings :
the same key as on the kiosks, under Kiosk Satellite \(-> Intercom.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use
.I file
for the settings instead of the default one (see
.BR FILES ).
One instance runs per settings file. Starting it again with the same file
brings up the running instance's window instead, and the other options are then
ignored. Separate files let several instances run side by side, each with its
own name and port.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mdns
Neither announce this computer on the network nor look for kiosks. Kiosks can
still be added by address.
.TP
.BI \-\-call " address"
Call a kiosk once it is reachable.
.I address
is its host, its host and port as
.IR host : port ,
or its name.
.TP
.B \-\-video
With
.B \-\-call
or
.BR \-\-auto\-answer :
with the camera on.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-answer
Answer incoming calls after a second.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH NETWORK
Calls come in on TCP port 2324, or the port set in
.BR Settings .
Kiosks are found over mDNS on UDP port 5353. With TLS on, calls come in
encrypted on the port after the plain one, 2325 by default. A firewall has to
let these ports in.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/intercom-satellite/settings.conf
The settings: name, intercom key, port, the kiosks added by address, their
names and symbols, and confirmed TLS certificates.
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is
.I ~/.config
unless set otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LANG ", " LANGUAGE
Choose the language. German and English are included.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/meiser79/intercom-satellite-desktop
.SH AUTHOR
Peter Meiser
